# PaceTasks

Expo (React Native) + TypeScript task app backed by Supabase. Anonymous
auth — no login screen, each device gets a stable Supabase user id via
`ensureSession()` in `src/lib/supabase.ts`. UI matches the "PaceTasks Film"
Claude Design: a light sage/cream theme with a forest-green accent (see
`src/lib/theme.ts`), plain white cards with no per-timing color coding, and
a text-only pill tab bar (see `App.tsx`'s `PillTabBar`).

## Structure

- `App.tsx` — root: waits for session, sets up the 3-tab navigator (Tasks / Stats / Settings) behind a custom `PillTabBar` (text-only, no icons).
- `src/screens/` — one file per tab screen. Screens own layout + hook wiring, no direct Supabase calls.
- `src/components/` — presentational pieces reused across screens (QuickAddBar, TaskItem, FocusSessionModal, EndOfDayCard, WeekHeatmap, DropdownPill, Stepper, StatCard). No data fetching here.
- `src/hooks/` — `useSession`, `useTasks`, `useSettings`. All Supabase reads/writes for a screen go through these, never inline in a component. `useTasks` also keeps its list live (Realtime INSERT/UPDATE filtered by user, unfiltered DELETE, silent reload on app foreground) and merges every change through `upsertTask`/`removeTask` so a local write and its Realtime echo never duplicate. Both `TaskListScreen` and `SettingsScreen` call `useSettings` independently (each screen owns its own data, per convention) rather than prop-drilling settings down from `App.tsx`.
- Brain Dump UI: `useBrainDump` (hook) drives `BrainDumpSheet` + `BrainDumpCandidateRow` (presentational). All transitions live in the pure reducer `src/lib/brainDumpState.ts` (unit-tested) — add new states/actions there, not in the hook. `src/lib/brainDumpApi.ts` is the only caller of the `brain-dump` Edge Function and the commit/discard RPCs; it always sends the phone's time zone (`src/lib/deviceContext.ts`). UI wording for issue codes and summaries lives in `src/lib/brainDumpCopy.ts`; due-day labels in `src/lib/dueLabel.ts`.
- `src/lib/tasksApi.ts` / `src/lib/settingsApi.ts` — the only files that call Supabase directly (besides `brainDumpApi.ts` for Brain Dump). Tasks are created only via `createTask(draft)` → `rpc("create_task")`; never insert into `tasks` directly, since Brain Dump and Siri share that one creation path.
- `supabase/functions/_shared/domain/` — pure, dependency-free TypeScript shared by the app (imported as `@domain/...`) and Edge Functions (Deno). `task.ts` (task model, enums, limits, `TaskDraft`), `dates.ts` (local date keys — "today" always comes from the phone), `todayTasks.ts` (what the Today list/Siri show), `taskCollection.ts`, `taskHistory.ts`. Relative imports inside it must use explicit `.ts` extensions and `import type` for types, or Deno breaks. Test fixtures live in `domain/testing/`.
- `src/lib/stats.ts` — pure functions only (no React, no network): `computeStats` (streaks/accuracy) and `buildWeekdayHeatmap` (the Stats tab's Mon-Fri × N-week grid).
- `@domain/taskHistory` — pure functions only, groups tasks by normalized (trimmed, lowercased) title. Powers quick-add autocomplete, the min/last/max time suggestions, and `TaskItem`'s range-timer bounds (`findExactMatch` looked up per task in `TaskListScreen`).
- `src/lib/categories.ts` — fixed list of task categories (`id`, `label`, `icon`, `color`). A task's `category` field stores a category `id` or `null` ("No category"). Add new categories here, never inline in a component.
- `src/components/DropdownPill.tsx` — generic one-tap choice control (Modal-based) used for the timing/time/category/scheduled-time pickers in `QuickAddBar`. Reuse it for any future "pick one of a few options" control.
- `src/components/TaskItem.tsx` — owns two independent timers: a manual actual-minutes stepper (always available via the checkbox) and, for tasks without a `scheduled_time`, a lightweight range timer (tap the minutes pill) that counts down from `suggestedMax` and flags "in range" once past `suggestedMin` — both props computed by the caller (`TaskListScreen`) from `taskHistory`, not fetched inside the component.
- `src/components/FocusSessionModal.tsx` — the Pomodoro countdown, opened from a task's FOCUS badge (shown when `task.scheduled_time` is set — mutually exclusive with the range timer). Reaching zero calls `onComplete` with `actual_minutes = workMinutes` — don't change that without considering the "estimate accuracy" stat, which depends on real actual-vs-estimated data.
- `src/lib/theme.ts` — single source of colors/spacing/radius/typography. Never hardcode a hex color or px value in a component; add it to `theme` instead.
- `supabase/functions/_shared/domain/brainDump/` — Brain Dump contract and rules, pure: `aiResult.ts` (zod schema the AI must satisfy; dates are *described* by the model, never computed), `resolveDate.ts`, `normalize.ts` (AI proposal → `TaskDraft`s using history, work hours, categories), `reviewPolicy.ts`, `types.ts` (API response). Category ids come from `@domain/categories`; `src/lib/categories.ts` only adds visuals.
- `supabase/functions/_shared/server/` — Deno-only (never imported by the app): `ai/` (vendor-neutral `LLMClient` + Anthropic/OpenAI adapters, `AIProvider` feature interface, versioned prompts — bump the prompt version on any prompt change), `brainDump/` (request schema, repository interface + Supabase impl, service, HTTP handler), `http/apiError.ts`. Tests use `node:assert/strict` + `Deno.test` (`deno task test` in `supabase/functions`).
- AI rule: AI output is a proposal. It is schema-validated and normalized, and tasks are only ever created via `create_task` (directly or through `commit_brain_dump`). AI never writes to the database, never picks ids or computes dates. API keys only live in Supabase secrets.
- `supabase/functions/_eval/` — evaluation set and runner for choosing/regressing AI models (`deno task eval`); not deployed.
- `supabase/migrations/` — source of truth for the DB schema, RLS policies and `public.create_task`. Never edit an applied migration; add a new timestamped file and mirror column/enum changes in `@domain/task`. DB tests live in `supabase/tests/database/` (pgTAP).
- Tests: `npm test` (Jest, pinned to Europe/Rome via `jest.globalSetup.js`), `npm run typecheck`, `npm run db:test`.

## Conventions

- Naming: `camelCase` for functions/variables, `PascalCase` for components/types, snake_case only for DB columns (matches Postgres/Supabase convention) — mirrored exactly in `@domain/task` (`Task`, `TaskDraft`) and re-exported from `src/lib/types.ts`.
- Every exported function/component gets a 1–2 sentence comment explaining *why*, not a restatement of the code.
- Timing values are always one of `"before_work" | "after_work" | "anytime"` (see `TaskTiming` in `@domain/task`) — don't introduce new string literals for this (or for priority, energy, due kind, source) without updating the type and the DB check constraint in a new migration.
- Dates: a task's `due_date` is a local calendar day (`"YYYY-MM-DD"`). Compute "today" with `toLocalDateKey(new Date())` from `@domain/dates` — never `toISOString().slice(0, 10)`, which is UTC.
- Category values are a category `id` from `src/lib/categories.ts` or `null` — always look categories up via `getCategory(id)` (handles `null` and unknown/deleted ids) rather than indexing `CATEGORIES` directly.
- A task's `scheduled_time` (`"HH:MM"` or `null`) is what enables Focus mode instead of the range timer — it's independent of `timing`; a task can have both a timing bucket and a fixed time.
- Keep screens dumb: fetching/mutation logic belongs in `src/hooks/*` or `src/lib/*Api.ts`, not inside a screen component.
- Icons: use `Ionicons` from `@expo/vector-icons`. The current design mostly avoids icons in favor of plain text (pills, tab bar) — only add an icon where the design shows one.
- Color: this design intentionally uses one green-based palette everywhere (no per-timing color coding on task rows) — category tags are the one place distinct accent hues (`theme.colors.indigo/purple/warning/pink`) are used, to tell categories apart at a glance.
